</span></td>
<td id="S3.T6.5.1.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.5.1.4.2.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_align_top" style="width:213.4pt;">
<span id="S3.T6.5.1.4.2.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S3.T6.5.1.4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">For small discrete counts (integers </span><math id="S3.T6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\leq 50" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo mathsize="0.500em">≤</mo><mn mathsize="0.500em">50</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\leq 50</annotation></semantics></math><span id="S3.T6.5.1.4.2.1.1.2" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">) of enumerable items, or quantities that are inherently exact and not subject to approximation (e.g., specific identifiers, fixed values in a sequence or definition, fundamental mathematical constants)</span></span>
</span></td>
<td id="S3.T6.5.1.4.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"><span id="S3.T6.5.1.4.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="font-size:50%;">89 (44%)</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S3.T6.5.1.5" class="ltx_tr">
<td id="S3.T6.5.1.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_align_top" style="padding-top:1pt;padding-bottom:1pt;"></td>
